cff-version: 1.2.0
title: DeepLST
message: >-
  Multi-modal and light-weight land surface temperature
  forecasting
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marieke
    family-names: Wesselkamp
    email: mwessel@bgc-jena.mpg.de
    affiliation: Max Planck Institute for Biogeochemistry
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2742-319X'
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.17605/OSF.IO/VYX8R
    description: Archived code of version 1.0.0 (tag DeepLST_v1.0.0)
abstract: >-
  Neural forecasting of land surface temperature (LST) over
  Africa from geostationary satellite observations (SEVIRI)
  and reanalysis (ERA5, ERA5-Land). An autoregressive MLP or
  transformer rolls the hourly LST state forward for up to
  ten days, driven by the large-scale atmospheric forcing.
  Forecasts are verified against climatology, persistence
  and ERA5-Land skin temperature.
keywords:
  - land surface forecasting
  - land surface temperature
  - autoregressive learning
